# Held's centralizing four-group: conditional assembly

The descendants reduce the kernel to two cyclic alternatives, exclude both
from an initial Section 4.1 nu seed, and prove that the supplied A₆ centralizes
mu and lambda. The seed's existence is still required before assembling the
contract whose additional inputs are just the symmetric extension and kernel
order four. No existence or source classification is asserted by this module.

Source: D. Held, Illinois J. Math. 13 (1969), 224–240,
DOI 10.1215/ijm/1256053756, Lemma 4.2, printed p.235.
-/
